    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1054">

                <pb facs="0911" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.112W892/30.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Carothers
                        to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gomez Palacio</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * Referring to enclosure, General
                    Villa is very anxious that you give the matter consideration, as he considers
                    that a great injustice is being done the country and the pacification retarded
                    by the fact that we insist that border towns be not attacked, at the same time
                    permitting the forces in possession of those towns to arm and equip
                    revolutionary forces from the United States. He is willing to have it work
                    against all factions, including himself.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. C. Carothers.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1054-a1.xml" xpointer="d1054-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
